Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:43:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: snapshot byte views and hex-encode on the consumer

Add LogHex for existing byte-string diagnostics so producer calls copy bytes
without allocating HexStr output. The view is consumed during Field(); the
record owns its snapshot. Saturated size causes full field omission, preserving
the existing bounded-record fields_truncated contract.

Add focused Logger/JSON tests comparing real HexStr output for empty and all
byte values after buffer mutation/release, plus oversized omission and a later
count field. These runtime tests are pending the coordinated normal build;
source lint and diff checks pass. This introduces no new secret logging.

Manual support API/test edits; formatting command:
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/logging/values.h src/test/logging_event_tests.cpp
